lines:
Don't force it: cut where it gives way;
the knife won't ever dull.
Brush off the earth, and never wash;
don't tug, and never pull.

bucket:
Planted! The bucket's yours to take:
the pond lies to the west;
go water all four, one by one;
the ground will do the rest.

wait:
Sand from the big lake to the south;
the ash from the fire, near;
and both together, in the furnace,
and glass will soon appear.
